/* Viewer for the validated balanced-imitation_20261019 public export. */
(()=>{const root='balanced-imitation-20261019/', $=s=>document.querySelector(s), el=(t,h)=>{const x=document.createElement(t);x.innerHTML=h;return x}, dl=p=>`<a href="${root}${p}" download>Download</a>`, fig=(p,c)=>`<figure><img loading="lazy" src="${root}${p}" alt="${c}"><figcaption>${c}. ${dl(p)}</figcaption></figure>`, read=x=>`<div class="how-to-read"><strong>How to read this.</strong> ${x}</div>`;
async function csv(p,caption){let r=await fetch(root+p),t=await r.text(),a=t.trim().split(/\r?\n/).map(x=>x.split(','));if(!a.length)return '';return `<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>${caption}</caption><thead><tr>${a[0].map(x=>`<th>${x}</th>`).join('')}</tr></thead><tbody>${a.slice(1).map(r=>`<tr>${r.map(x=>`<td>${x}</td>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>${dl(p)}</p>`}
const origin=x=>`<p class="origin-line">Origin: ${x}</p>`;
const section=el('section',`<div class="balanced-imitation" id="balanced-imitation"><h2>Balanced imitation: reproduction, noise null and analogue</h2><p>This section asks three questions in order: <strong>Can we reproduce the paper’s Fig. 4?</strong> <strong>Is its pattern more than noise?</strong> <strong>Does it hold when diversity is measured differently here?</strong> It is a viewer for validated exports; it performs no analysis.</p><details open><summary>What Fig. 4h shows, and what differs in this project</summary>${origin('Paper source data')}<p>Each line joins a tutor’s diversity to the mean diversity of its pupils; red means pupils higher and blue lower. The paper’s Shannon entropy is over ten colony-wide, fixed vocal states (ceiling 3.32 bits); its panel is descriptive and its causal interpretation relies on other panels.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Paper measurement compared with this project</caption><thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Paper</th><th>This project</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Categories</td><td>10 fixed colony-wide states</td><td>Family-local HDBSCAN, variable and not homologous</td></tr><tr><td>Unit</td><td>10 ms windows, time-weighted</td><td>Segmented whole syllables</td></tr><tr><td>Sample</td><td>6–8 s; 900–11,476 windows</td><td>104 to &gt;5,000 syllables</td></tr><tr><td>Ceiling</td><td>Shared log2(10)=3.32</td><td>Family-specific; also H/log2(Kfamily)</td></tr><tr><td>Range</td><td>2.3–3.3 bits</td><td>about 0.2–4.8 raw bits</td></tr><tr><td>Fitting</td><td>Population states</td><td>Tutor+pupils jointly fitted</td></tr><tr><td>Noise</td><td>Not applicable</td><td>Included versus assigned-only treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Coverage</td><td>68 tutors, 159 pairs</td><td>56 historical; 43 LR=200 t-SNE</td></tr><tr><td>Extra measures</td><td>Similarity, influence, mixed models</td><td>Hopkins, JSD overlap, noise treatments</td></tr></tbody></table></div>${read('What it does not show: that the two diversity measurements are interchangeable.')}</details><details open id="bi-paper"><summary>Reproduction of Fig. 4c–h</summary>${origin('Paper source data')}${fig('task1_paper_reproduction/fig4_reproduction_c_to_h.png','Reproduction of Fig. 4 panels c–h from the published workbook')}${fig('task1_paper_reproduction/fig4h_variants_mean_vs_pooled.png','Fig. 4h variants: mean pupils, pooled pupils, and their comparison')}<div data-csv="task1_paper_reproduction/reproduction_vs_paper.csv" data-caption="Reproduction versus paper"></div><p>208 birds (workbook; article text says 228), 68 tutors and 159/160 pairs. DG1→Aq32 has no counts. Panels a–b need unavailable raw features. The reported 42% reversals is not reproduced (32–38% under plausible definitions) and remains an open question*.</p>${read('Expect agreement to two decimals: this validates the workbook and entropy definition, not the paper’s causal interpretation.')}</details><details open id="bi-null"><summary>Statistical framing and noise null</summary>${origin('New analysis')}<p>The estimand is the movement of a pupil’s true diversity with its tutor’s true diversity: faithful copying plus independent deviations gives β=1; a pull toward the colony gives β&lt;1. Measurement error, autocorrelation, regression to the mean, ceiling effects, shared families and unequal pupil counts can all fake attenuation; the null explicitly scans those sampling effects.</p>${fig('task2_noise_null/fig_null_scan_over_tau.png','Simplex-null scan over effective autocorrelation τ')}${fig('task2_noise_null/fig_null_histograms.png','Observed statistics against simplex-null simulations')}${fig('task2_noise_null/fig_pull_sweep.png','Pull-parameter sweep')}${fig('task2_noise_null/fig_noise_and_prior_checks.png','Noise and prior checks')}<div data-csv="task2_noise_null/simplex_null_by_tau.csv" data-caption="Simplex null by effective autocorrelation τ"></div><div data-csv="task2_noise_null/scalar_null_by_tau.csv" data-caption="Scalar null cross-check"></div><p>Null A draws tutor state distributions from a fitted Dirichlet prior, samples counts at n/τ, and models faithful imperfect copying (w=0); a pull model adds colony weight w. τ is bounded at 10–50 by design and observed tutor–pupil divergence. Reversal share is compatible with noise at every τ and is not evidence.</p>${read('If the pattern were sampling noise, observed values would lie in the blue bands. The null does not establish genetic, age, housing, or partition causes.')}</details><details open id="bi-analogue"><summary>The analogue on this project’s entropies</summary>${origin('New analysis')}<p>Pre-declared display: noise-included, fraction 0.01; PCoA-, UMAP-, PHATE-Euclidean historical settings and GPU-native LR=200 t-SNE-Euclidean. Primary scale is H/log2(Kfamily), tutor versus equal-weight mean pupil; this does not declare the Stage S7 primary setting.</p>${fig('task3_analogue/fig_analogue_4h_family_lines.png','Family-line analogue across four illustrative embeddings')}${fig('task3_analogue/fig_analogue_4d_pairs.png','Pair-level analogue; pairs sharing a tutor are not independent')}${fig('task3_analogue/fig_multiverse_normalized.png','All 42 normalised specifications')}${fig('task3_analogue/fig_multiverse_raw.png','All 42 raw-bit specifications')}<div data-csv="task3_analogue/multiverse_specification_curve.csv" data-caption="42-setting multiverse specification curve"></div>${fig('task3b_robustness/fig_robustness_matched_and_agreement.png','Matched-family and cross-embedding robustness')}${read('Historical settings are consistent with the paper-direction pattern; LR=200 t-SNE is not distinguishable from its sampling-noise null. Shared partitions and weak cross-embedding agreement remain important limitations.')}<div class="conclusion"><strong>Status: partially replicated, not established. In all 30 historical settings (PCoA, UMAP, PHATE) pupils' mean entropy depends on the tutor's entropy with a slope of 0.06-0.50, close to the paper's 0.36, and the contrast between low- and high-diversity tutors (0.12 normalised) is larger than sampling noise predicts. In the 12 LR=200 t-SNE settings the slope is 0.59-0.95 and indistinguishable from the sampling-noise null. The sampling-noise null does not cover partition instability: tutor entropy agrees poorly across embeddings, so the attenuation could also reflect measurement unreliability of tutor entropy; instrumental-variable estimates are too imprecise to decide. This analysis supports the direction of the paper's pattern under three of four measurement choices; it does not yet prove it holds when diversity is measured differently.</strong></div></details><details><summary>Open tasks*</summary><p>Fixed-state analogue*; partition-instability null*; Fig. 4e–g analogues*; effective τ*; hierarchical lineage model*; foster-pupil and age/date covariates*; paper’s reversal definition*; PCA settings* (fewer than 20 families).</p></details></div>`);
Promise.all([...section.querySelectorAll('[data-csv]')].map(async d=>d.innerHTML=await csv(d.dataset.csv,d.dataset.caption))).then(()=>{}); const after=$('#lineage-targets'); after?.after(section); const toc=$('.sidebox');toc?.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<a href="#balanced-imitation">Balanced imitation</a>'); const review=$('#needs-review');review?.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<li><strong>Balanced imitation test:</strong> partially replicated; partition instability not yet modelled.</li>');document.head.append(el('style','.balanced-imitation{padding:1.2rem;margin:1rem 0;border:1px solid #b9ced0;border-radius:12px;background:#fbfdfd}.balanced-imitation img{max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #d8e2e4}.balanced-imitation table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.88rem}.balanced-imitation th,.balanced-imitation td{padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid #d8e2e4;text-align:left}.balanced-imitation .conclusion{padding:1rem;background:#eff8f6;border-left:4px solid #087f79}.how-to-read{padding:.7rem;background:#eff8f6;border-left:4px solid #087f79}'))})();
